Z||000012||grinthock||07-25-2001||10:36 PM||||WOW!! Finally a rear mod that I like --- What kind of price are we talkin?||||reg||1
Z||000013||AusFiero||07-25-2001||10:49 PM||||Well basically Grinthock I do not know price yet. I have to build it an evaluate the tooling expenses etc. But I am building it. Price wise I know will be good for your market based on what I have seen around for sale and the different values in our dollar to the USA. Manufacturing here is cheap compared to the USA. <P>A full Stage-2 body kit for instance, front, rear, sides, skirts,  back, all lights and fittings  etc is gunna make a full ISMA kit look very poor in comparison price wise. I will probably be also dealing exclusively through a USA outlet who will have better advertising and promotional powers than I have from here. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000014||Pontiaddict||07-26-2001||02:16 AM||||Looks Great Aus!<BR>I think the lettering has to be red. I know Clear is illegal to have facing backward (not including backup lights, and I think orange is too except for turn signals).||||reg||14
Z||000015||AusFiero||07-26-2001||02:53 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pontiaddict:<BR><B>Looks Great Aus!<BR>I think the lettering has to be red. I know Clear is illegal to have facing backward (not including backup lights, and I think orange is too except for turn signals).</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks for the advice Pontiaddict. We are allowed to have clear or orange lights showing here. <BR>What about all the other states in the USA? <P>Had even considered black. Black lettering with white high intensity globes behind for a charcoal blacklight effct.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000016||AusFiero||07-26-2001||07:53 AM||||Ok I am testing a few other options here. I have decided for the non lip spoiler modela trim panel probably doesn't look to bad and would be a lot less work for myself and anyone trying to fit it. Also what about reversing lights there?  Just trying a wing design out too. Wings are hard to draw from the rear so I hope it portrays what I am actually thinking anyway.<P>Comments? Particulrly on the trim and wing as I am unsure on both. <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stage2rear04.jpg"> <BR>with black trim panel<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stage2rear05.jpg"> <BR>or body colour trim panel<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stage2rear06.jpg"> <BR>with lip spoiler and trim panel<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||TI_3VOM||07-26-2001||02:29 PM||||Aus,<BR>   Love the lip spoiler and trim panel. Here's a couple of suggestions for the back-up lights: install them in the bumper in place of the reflectors, or widen the area where the rear license plate mounts and install them there, flanking the rear plate. <P>BTW, are custom inserts possible. Say, instead of Pontiac, it would say Fiero, in fiero script, no less?   ||||reg||14
Z||000018||FieroGTguy||07-26-2001||03:41 PM||||Would you sell a tail light conversion without lettering for a badgeless look?  I'm thinking with the body kit and a choptop...  It would be fun to puzzle the public.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Also, if not badgeless...  Can you make it up to the buyer what it says?  Just sell template lettering with the badgeless product so we can have whatever 6 letters light up what we want?  (so we might see one light up "MODFYD", "AUSRLZ", or something like that)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Greg||||reg||1
Z||000019||mrgone||07-26-2001||04:42 PM||||or... EATRICE||||reg||1
Z||000020||AusFiero||07-26-2001||06:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TI_3VOM:<BR><B>Aus,<BR>   Love the lip spoiler and trim panel. Here's a couple of suggestions for the back-up lights: install them in the bumper in place of the reflectors, <BR>BTW, are custom inserts possible. Say, instead of Pontiac, it would say Fiero, in fiero script, no less?   </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>See the first Pics. They are in that spot  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I kinda like them there too.<BR>hmm on the lettering. I was going to mould the Pontiac into the panel and have individual cut letters made to fit flush in recesses. but I suppose with a fluro lit light box behind and a rectangle sheet of reflective material supplied in red it wouldn't be hard to cut any lettering at all out. I wouldn't do the letter cutting though as the edge of each letter would have to be sanded to shape then rounded off to look right otherwise it would look tacky with square edged holes around the lettering.  That would up costs way to much if I had to spend heaps of extra time on each panel. <BR>Though I think the latter will be the option. I can see some people kinda liking their cars name etc across the back. <BR>All this input helps. I want this kit to be perfect, and adaptable and I am sure people wont mind a little cutting and sanding to have any words they want.  <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000021||FieroGTguy||07-26-2001||07:10 PM||||Further input:<P>I would definitely go with the back up lights where the rear reflectors are.  Less work, and it looks better.<P>I love the exhaust tip idea.  What tips would fit that configuration?<P>And, I personally wouldn't mind the fiberglass work to add the lip to a decklid with the stock spoiler.  I am quite fond of my spoiler.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Greg||||reg||1
Z||000022||AusFiero||07-26-2001||07:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroGTguy:<BR><B>Further input:<P>I would definitely go with the back up lights where the rear reflectors are.  Less work, and it looks better.<P>I love the exhaust tip idea.  What tips would fit that configuration?<P>And, I personally wouldn't mind the fiberglass work to add the lip to a decklid with the stock spoiler.  I am quite fond of my spoiler.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Greg</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have access to square exhaust outlets (aftermarket) like that here in Australia Greg. they would be part of the kit as will every piece needed to mount it and finish your car including grills etc. All people will need to do is paint and fit the parts.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000023||GarethWright||07-26-2001||09:38 PM||||What are the grills around the exhaust pipes going to be made of? If they are heat resistent enough, would it be possible to have an uncut grill with the exhaust pipes flush with the back of it, for a smoother look?  Have there been posts with drawings of the front/sides or is this the first?<BR>Keep up the good work,<BR>Gareth||||reg||1
Z||000024||grinthock||07-26-2001||09:57 PM||||I like the whole idea -- but i like the lip spoiler the best -- I am a blank Fiero Trunk Fan.||||reg||1
Z||000025||AusFiero||07-26-2001||10:13 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GarethWright:<BR><B>What are the grills around the exhaust pipes going to be made of? If they are heat resistent enough, would it be possible to have an uncut grill with the exhaust pipes flush with the back of it, for a smoother look?  Have there been posts with drawings of the front/sides or is this the first?<BR>Keep up the good work,<BR>Gareth</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The mesh grills will be metal and could be left closed as an option. <BR>Yes there is designs of the front and sides. The side version has been done on a coupe but you will get the idea. Coupe and fastback versions will be available. Fastback will be released first. Sorry coupe guys but I just found out my coupe that was coming to Australia isn't coming anymore so I need to sell some fastback kits first to finance buying a coupe myself now. Which isn't exactly cheap to do in this country. I will have quite a large capital outlay in this at it is.<P>Here are the links to the other views for those who have not seen the threads before.<P><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/007445.html" TARGET=_blank>FRONT VIEW</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/007274.html" TARGET=_blank>SIDE VIEW</A><P>Rear pictures of the coupe version will be online in the next couple of days and I will post them in this thread.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> |||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000026||b lo 0||07-27-2001||12:02 AM||||I love it so far (you guys actually have Skylines-you SUCK!!!  I've wanted a GTR for years!)<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="1">'85 GT (in progress)<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">       <BR>White Lightnin!  (NOT moonshine, for all you hillbillies!)</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by b lo 0 (edited 07-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000027||AusFiero||07-29-2001||09:39 AM||||Ok The first version is the go with the lip spoiler. Anyone who wants to use a stock rear wing or a potential one I may bring out will have to go with a trim panel. I feel a glassed on bit on the decklid would not be strong enough and I don't want people blaming me for them using a bad glass guy or doing a bad job moulding it in themselves. Plus I am trying to keep this whole kit as a bolt on operation for the home handyman who only has a drill and some basic hand tools. <P>That is why I have even decided to make the complete doorskins rather than bits that mould onto them. Well still considering a half doorskin that can bolt on and be hidden by the body moulding. <P>Reversing lamps will stay in the stock reflector locations.<P>The Fastback kit will be released first.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||14
Z||000028||Formula||07-29-2001||10:40 AM||||will you sell the parts seperate so I could put the door skins, front nose, and rear nose on my coupe/formula?<p>[This message has been edited by Formula (edited 07-29-2001).]||||reg||1
